Analysis:
"quantum computing" does not exist in doc.txt. Two problems were exposed:

PROBLEM 1 — No relevance threshold
  Retrieval always returns top-k regardless of relevance. All three scores
  (0.76, 0.76, 0.75) are similar — meaning nothing matched well, but the
  system sent irrelevant context to the LLM anyway.

  Fix: Add a minimum score threshold (e.g. 0.80). If no chunk scores above
  the threshold, pass empty context or skip generation entirely.

  Where to fix: retrieve_topk() in main.c — after scoring, count how many
  hits are above the threshold. If zero, set out_context to NULL and skip
  llm_generate().

PROBLEM 2 — No "I don't know" instruction
  The prompt tells TinyLlama to "use the following context to answer the
  question" but does not tell it what to do when the context is irrelevant.
  Small models like TinyLlama hallucinate when they have nothing real to say.

  Fix: Update the system prompt in llm.c to add:
  "If the context does not contain enough information to answer, say
  'I don't know'."

  Where to fix: the tmpl string in llm_generate() in llm.c.
